1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,017
Welcome back. Settle in and take a breath that's a little deeper than the last.

2
00:00:05,057 --> 00:00:08,600
Today, you'll write your personal AI-use charter –

3
00:00:08,640 --> 00:00:11,645
a short set of promises to yourself.

4
00:00:11,685 --> 00:00:13,367
Start with your worksheet's ladder.

5
00:00:13,407 --> 00:00:15,467
It goes from no AI,

6
00:00:15,507 --> 00:00:17,075
to AI for ideas,

7
00:00:17,115 --> 00:00:18,747
to AI as a tutor,

8
00:00:18,787 --> 00:00:21,949
all the way to open AI exploration.

9
00:00:21,989 --> 00:00:23,884
For each class or task,

10
00:00:23,924 --> 00:00:27,198
where do you want to be and what does your instructor allow?

11
00:00:27,238 --> 00:00:29,680
Now, finish these lines in your own words,

12
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,497
“AI helps my learning when...”

13
00:00:32,553 --> 00:00:34,527
“AI replaces my learning when…”

14
00:00:35,609 --> 00:00:37,913
“Before I trust an AI answer, I will...”

15
00:00:38,988 --> 00:00:40,715
Let's also name something real.

16
00:00:40,755 --> 00:00:45,000
A lot of students worry about being falsely accused of using AI.

17
00:00:45,040 --> 00:00:47,355
If that's you, you're not alone.

18
00:00:47,395 --> 00:00:49,803
Keeping drafts and notes protects you,

19
00:00:49,843 --> 00:00:52,572
and if your charter matches what your instructor allows,

20
00:00:52,612 --> 00:00:55,627
you can use AI with a clear conscience.

21
00:00:55,666 --> 00:00:57,750
Read your charter back slowly.

22
00:00:57,790 --> 00:00:59,404
Does it sound like you?

23
00:00:59,444 --> 00:01:01,192
Does it feel honest?

24
00:01:01,232 --> 00:01:04,608
You can revise it anytime.
